Note ordering subtlety in commit: I debit+increment nonce on from first, then credit to. Deterministic given fixed order. Fine.

One more nuance: gate_open checked AFTER funds — order of checks defines which Refusal surfaces when multiple violated; document precedence: existence → nonce → funds → gate → floor. Deterministic error taxonomy matters for cross-node agreement on refusal reasons too (if refusals are logged to consensus-visible receipts). Since refusal produces no root change, reasons can differ across nodes harmlessly — but keep deterministic anyway.

